id: pm-1eww
title: Preview preset stacks through host profile composition
description: "Adapt selected bundled preset contributions into a host profile application plan. Expose competing ownership of settings leaves, template names and seed identities; require explicit owner choices, compose disjoint contributions deterministically, canonicalize equivalent reordered selections, and never write during preview. Reuse core profile planning and audited settings normalization rather than add a composition engine or duplicate single-preset capability negotiation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: composition,planning,presets,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-26T01:18:10.503Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T01:41:53.669Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Conflicting leaves require explicit choices; disjoint contributions compose deterministically; reordered equivalent selections produce the same canonical plan; preview writes nothing; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON and actionable refusals; seeded model-based and adversarial validation; read-only public tracker evidence; npm and Bun release gates pass in CI.
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T01:18:47.711Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: core SDK exports ProjectProfileDefinition, planProfileApplication, describeProjectProfile and lintProjectProfile. Core profile config covers registered descriptors but not every preset governance/testing/validation leaf; the adapter must use host audited includePreview normalization for those settings. Sibling source/README search found no preset stack adapter. Existing presets plan is single-preset feature capability negotiation and remains separate. Scope: preview only, no apply/recovery journal, import/export/sync mutation, status classification, leases or outbox. Test snapshots through the SDK and byte fingerprints to prove preview cannot change native fields or relationships."
  "2026-10-26T01:30:54.930Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the typed planPresetStack/summarizePresetStack SDK and presets stack command. Catalog ownership is canonical by preset/path; equal values coalesce, conflicting settings/template/seed identities need explicit competing owners. Core planProfileApplication owns template/config classification. Host SDK dry-run unexpectedly needs a workspace lock even for preview: normalization now runs on a mode-0600 settings copy in a disposable mode-0700 directory, removed in finally; source trackers remain untouched and can be read-only. Public main snapshot 6046edb: 80 items, 166 files, 1315278 bytes; 91 plans (64 ready, 21 unresolved, 6 normalization refusals), 21 canonical reordered pairs, max compact JSON 3249 bytes, 1440.42 ms; exact SHA-256 unchanged. Initial randomized verification used get, which records derived usage; replaced verification reads with authoritative SDK locateItem/readLocatedItem and readSettings, with all source bytes retained in the assertion."
  "2026-10-26T01:35:12.663Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: changed only planPresetStack conflict detection to accept competing values automatically. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"competing settings\" tests/stack.test.ts failed (1 test, expected ready false but received true; exit 1). Restored the exact function and rebuilt. Targeted source coverage now measures both new modules at 100% lines, branches and functions (9 focused tests). Scratch normalization copies raw source settings and lets the real SDK validate them: permissive readSettings defaults no longer disguise an invalid tracker. Public read-only validation repeated successfully with unchanged SHA-256; 91 plans and 3249-byte maximum output. No package lint script or eslint dependency exists; run the canonical pinned pm-ops lint policy using disposable lint dependencies, keeping the package pins unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T01:37:46.805Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted linked-test run passed 11/11, zero failures/skips: node --test tests/stack.test.ts tests/stack-cli.test.ts (run through pm test --run --progress --timeout 300). Includes seed 0x51ac0ffe, 500 randomized sequences and 2000 previews, older-input replay, JSON/CRLF variants, all seven settings catalogs, templates/seeds, and SDK-read native documents with parent relationships, files, docs, comments, tags, priority and bodies; exact source bytes remain unchanged. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run docstring passed. Canonical pm-ops@2026.10.20 runLintGate passed all 7 changed TypeScript files using isolated ESLint 10.10.0 and Babel parser 8.0.5; no dependency pins changed. Full npm/Bun release evidence will come from CI as requested; no local full gate was run."
  "2026-10-26T01:41:51.823Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/162 . Implementation commit 75c2b2437cafed491119171fce8f7a384ca86edd passed CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/actions/runs/40255269279 : npm run release:check 208/208, bun run release:check 208/208; zero failed/skipped tests in either. Both measured 25 source files at 100% lines, branches and functions, with unchanged thresholds. Node 22 and 26 coverage jobs, Windows lifecycle and CodeQL also passed. Isolated-home strict tracker health passed; the ordinary host had a global pm-github 2026.10.25 vs pinned host 2026.10.20 skew, so no package pins were changed. Review availability is separate from CI: Greptile trial ended; CodeRabbit manual review required; Cubic and Sourcery skipped. No substantive external approval is claimed. Acceptance criteria are met; leave the item open for orchestrator verification. SDK gap observed, not filed: settings dryRun requires a lock/writeable tracker even though it does not persist settings; disposable SDK normalization keeps this feature read-only on its source."
